Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?stmp3770/hp39gii:=20add=20NuttX=20SoC=20port=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20boots=20NSH=20in=20EmuGII=20QEMU?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ARM926EJ-S SoC port for the HP 39gII (Sigmatel STMP3770, 512KB on-chip
SRAM, no external DRAM). Verified in the EmuGII QEMU stmp3770 machine:
NSH shell, LCD panel (LCDIF + APBH DMA), ICOLL interrupts, TIMROT tick,
and the 11x5 keyboard matrix all work end-to-end (keys reach NSH).

- stmp3770_memorymap.h: register bases taken from real-hardware probing [M]
- core drivers: ICOLL/TIMROT/PL011/clkctrl/heap (no MMU for bring-up)
- LCD driver ported from ExistOS (hw/regs* headers + compat shims)
- keyboard: GPIO matrix scan + keycode->ASCII + console injection
  (ECHO side-channel and CONSOLE feed, selectable and co-exist)
- board hp39gii: nsh defconfig, ld.script, elftosb boot-stream tooling

Key fix for the keyboard->NSH path: arm_serialinit() must call
pl011_earlyserialinit() before pl011_serialinit(), so uart_register()
initialises ECHO/ICANON/ICRNL; otherwise reads run raw and NSH never
echoes or parses input.
